From the  $AM-GM$  inequality, we get
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{b}+\frac{b}{c}+\frac{c}{d}+\frac{d}{a}+\frac{4bd}{ac}&=\frac{a}{b}+\frac{c}{d}+\frac{ab+cd+4bd}{ac}
&\ge3\sqrt[3]{\frac{ab+cd+4bd}{bd}}
&=3\sqrt[3]{\frac{a}{d}+\frac{c}{b}+4}
\end{align*}
So, it suffices to show  $\frac{a}{d}+\frac{c}{b}\ge4$ . But, this is straightforward by using Cauchy-Schwarz and the problem condition.  $$ \left(\frac{a}{d}+\frac{c}{b}\right)(ad+bc)\ge(a+c)^2\implies\frac{a}{d}+\frac{c}{b}\ge\frac{(a+c)^2}{ad+bc}=4 $$  For the equality case, just notice that  $\frac{\frac{a}{d}}{ad}=\frac{\frac{c}{b}}{bc}\Longleftrightarrow b=d$  must hold for the equality case in Cauchy-Schwarz. For the equality case in  $AM-GM$  we have  $\frac{a}{b}=\frac{c}{d}\implies a=c$ . For equality to hold, we must have equality in all of the above inequalities. Replacing  $a=c=x$  and  $b=d=y$  and using  $\frac{a}{d}+\frac{c}{b}\ge4$  we have  $$ 2\frac{x}{y}=4\implies x=2y $$  So, equality holds iff  $(a,b,c,d)=(2t,t,2t,t)$ , where  $t$  is a positive real number. We easily check that this satisfies the equality and the problem condition.

