Let  $O$  be the center of the semicircle. Furthermore, let  $EX$  and  $FY$  intersect at  $G$ . Finally, let  $AO$  intersect  $EX$  at  $H$  and  $FY$  at  $I$ . It suffices to show that  $\angle BAG=90-\angle B$ .

Observe that  $\angle BOF=90-\angle B$  from right triangle  $BOF$  and  $OF=OY$  by the definition of circle; hence  $\angle XYF=45-\frac{B}{2}$ . Similarly  $\angle YXE=45-\frac{C}{2}$ . Hence  $\angle EGY=90-\frac{B}{2}-\frac{C}{2}=\frac{A}{2}$  by Triangle Angle Sum. It follows that quadrilateral  $AFGH$  is cyclic.

