We have 
\begin{align*}
PF^2 &= AF^2 + AP^2 - 2AF\cdot AP \cos \angle DAB
RF^2 &= BF^2 + BR^2 - 2BF\cdot BR \cos \angle CBA.
\end{align*}

We claim that  $PF = RF$ , thus we need to show that 
\begin{align*}
AP^2 - BR^2 &= AB\cdot AP\cos DAB - AB\cos BR\cos CBA
&= AB\cdot AP\left(\frac{AB^2+AD^2-BD^2}{2AB\cdot AD}\right) - AB\cdot BR \left(\frac{AB^2+BC^2 - AC^2}{2AB\cdot BC}\right)
&= \left(\frac{AP(AB^2+AD^2-BD^2)}{2AD}\right) - \left(\frac{BR(AB^2+BC^2-AC^2)}{2BC}\right).
\end{align*}

Notice that \[\frac{AP}{AD} = \frac{AE}{AD} = \frac{BE}{BC} = \frac{BR}{BC}.\] Thus we need to show that 
\begin{align*}
AP^2 - BR^2 &= \left(\frac{AP(AB^2+AD^2-BD^2)}{2AD}\right) - \left(\frac{BR(AB^2+BC^2-AC^2)}{2BC}\right)
&= \frac{AP}{2AD}(AB^2+AD^2-BD^2-AB^2-BC^2+AC^2)
&= \frac{AP}{2AD}(AD^2+AC^2-BD^2-BC^2).
\end{align*}

Now \[\frac{AP^2}{AD^2} = \frac{BR^2}{BC^2} = \frac{AP^2-BR^2}{AD^2-BC^2}.\]

Thus we need to show that \[\frac{AP^2}{AD^2}\cdot (AD^2-BC^2) = \frac{AP}{2AD}(AD^2+AC^2-BD^2-BC^2)\] or \[\frac{2AP}{AD} - 1 = \frac{AC^2-BD^2}{AD^2-BC^2}.\]

Now let  $\angle EAD = \alpha, \angle EDA = \beta, \angle EDC = A, \angle ECD = B$ . Notice that we have  $A+B = 180 - (\alpha + \beta)$ . 

We have 
\begin{align*}
\frac{2AP}{AD} - 1 &= \frac{2\cdot AE \cos \alpha \sin \beta}{AE \sin (\alpha + \beta)} - 1
&= \frac{\sin(\alpha+\beta)+\sin(\beta - \alpha)}{\sin(\alpha+\beta)}-1
&=\frac{\sin(\beta - \alpha)}{\sin(\alpha+\beta)}.
\end{align*}

Now 
\begin{align*}
\frac{AC^2-BD^2}{AD^2-BC^2}&= \frac{\sin^2 (A+\beta) - \sin^2 (B+\beta)}{\sin^2 B - \sin^2 A}
&=\frac{\sin(A+\beta + B + \beta)\sin(A+\beta - B - \beta)}{\sin (B+A)\sin (B-A)}
&= -\frac{\sin(A+B+2\beta)}{\sin(A+B)}
&= -\frac{\sin (180 - \alpha - \beta + 2\beta}{\sin(180 - \alpha - \beta)}
&= - \frac{\sin(180 - \alpha + \beta)}{\sin (\alpha+\beta)}
&=\frac{\sin (\beta - \alpha)}{\sin(\alpha+\beta)} = \frac{2AP}{AD} - 1.
\end{align*}

Thus we have  $PF = RF$ . We also have from cyclic quadrilaterals, \[\angle EQP = \angle QRE.\] Thus  $QF$  is external angle bisector of  $\angle PQF$ . We showed that  $PF = RF$ . Now either  $PQ = QR$  or  $P,Q,R,F$  are concyclic. If  $PQ = RQ$ , then  $R\equiv F$  and we are anyways done. 

Thus  $P,Q,R,F$  are concyclic and we are done.

