Having drawn the diagram, let  $\omega $  be the unit circle and let  $F-O-G$  be the real axis, where  $f=1$  and  $g=-1$ . Here, we assume that WLOG we draw the tangent to  $\omega$  at point  $F.$  Let  $M=m, N=n, R=r, Q=q$ . For all points  $Z=z$  on the unit circle we have that  $z\overline{z}=1.$   Since  $AQ$  and  $AM$  are tangent to  $\omega$ , we have that   $$ a=\frac{2qm}{q+m} \hspace{2mm} \text{and} \hspace{2mm} \overline{a}=\frac{2}{q+m}. $$  Similarly, we know that   $$ b=\frac{2mn}{m+n} \hspace{2mm} \text{and} \hspace{2mm} \overline{b}=\frac{2}{m+n}, $$    $$ c=\frac{2rn}{r+n} \hspace{2mm} \text{and} \hspace{2mm} \overline{c}=\frac{2}{r+n}, $$    $$ d=\frac{2qr}{q+r} \hspace{2mm} \text{and} \hspace{2mm} \overline{d}=\frac{2}{q+r}. $$  From  $AC\perp FO$ , we get that   $$ \frac{a-c}{f-0}=-\overline{\left(\frac{a-c}{f-0}\right)}  $$    $$ \frac{\frac{2mq}{m+q}-\frac{2nr}{n+r}}{f}=-\frac{\frac{2}{m+q}-\frac{2}{n+r}}{\frac{1}{f}} $$    $$ \frac{mq(n+r)-nr(m+q)}{f(m+q)(n+r)}=-\frac{(n+r-m-q)f}{(m+q)(n+r)} $$    $$ mq(n+r)-nr(m+q)=m+q-n-r $$  Now we will calculate  $P=p$ . Note that  $P$  satisfies the following two conditions:  $PF\perp FO$  and  $P\in BD$ . From the first condition it follows that   $$ \frac{p-f}{f-0}=-\overline{\left(\frac{p-f}{f-0}\right)}\iff $$    $$ \iff p-1=-(\overline{p}-1) \iff p-1 = 1-\overline{p}\iff \overline{p}=2-p. $$   From the second condition it follows that   $$ \frac{d-p}{d-b}=\overline{\left(\frac{d-p}{d-b}\right)}\iff $$     $$ \iff\frac{\frac{2rq}{r+q}-p}{\frac{2rq}{r+q}-\frac{2mn}{m+n}}=\frac{\frac{2}{r+q}+p-2}{\frac{2}{r+q}-\frac{2}{m+n}}\iff $$    $$ \iff\frac{2rq-p(r+q)}{rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}=\frac{2+p(r+q)-2(r+q)}{m+n-r-q}\iff $$    $$ p(r+q)(m+n-r-q+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q))=  $$     $$ =2rq(m+n-r-q)-2rq(m+n)+2mn(r+q)+2(r+q)(rq(m+n)-mn(r+q))= $$    $$ =(r+q)(-2rq+2mn+2rq(m+n)-2mn(r+q)) \iff $$     $$ \iff p=2\cdot\frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)} $$  Since  $PT$  and  $PF$  are tangents to  $\omega$ , we have that   $$ p=\frac{2ft}{f+t}\iff t=\frac{pf}{2f-p}=\frac{p}{2-p}. $$   Hence, 

\begin{align*}
t &= \frac{2\cdot\frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}}{2-2\cdot\frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}} 
  &= \frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)-mn+rq-rq(m+n)+mn(r+q)} 
  &= \frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q-mn+rq} 
\end{align*}

We wish to show that  $PT$  is tangent to  $(ACT)$ , i.e. we wish to show that   $$ \angle ACT = \angle ATP \iff \arg\left(\frac{a-c}{t-c}\right)=\arg\left(\frac{a-t}{p-t}\right) \iff $$     $$ \iff \arg\left(\frac{(a-c)(p-t)}{(t-c)(a-t)}\right)=0 \iff $$     $$ \iff \frac{(a-c)(p-t)}{(t-c)(a-t)}=\overline{\left(\frac{(a-c)(p-t)}{(t-c)(a-t)}\right)}. $$  Now we can calculate
\begin{align*}
    t-c &= \frac{mn-rq+rq(m+n)-mn(r+q)}{m+n-r-q-mn+rq} - \frac{2rn}{r+n}
    &= \frac{(r+n)(mn-rq+rqm+rqn-mnr-mnq)-2rn(m+n-r-q-mn+rq)}{(r+n)(m+n-r-q-mn+rq)} 
