[/asy]**<span style="color:#00f">Claim 2.</span>** $\angle AA_1D_A=\angle MAA^*$ *Proof.* From claim 1 it follows that  $\angle DA'A=\angle XSA=\angle MSA$ . And since  $(AA', AM)$  and  $(AH, AO)$  are pairs of isogonal lines in  $ABC$  it follows that \[\angle DAA'=\angle HAA'=\angle OAM=\angle MAS,\]
so  $\triangle DAA'\sim \triangle MAS$ . As  $D_A$  and  $O$  are the midpoints of  $AA'$  and  $AS$ , respectively, it follows that  $\triangle DAD_A\sim\triangle MAO$ , and since by the Midline theorem  $\triangle DAD_A\sim\triangle A_1AA'$  it follows that  $\triangle A_1AA'\sim\triangle MAO$ . And again, since  $D_A$  and  $Q$  are the midpoints of  $AA'$  and  $AO$ , respectively, this implies that  $\triangle A_1AD_A\sim \triangle MAQ$ , so  $\angle AA_1D_A=\angle AMQ$ . 
